# Build output
build/
app/build/
.gradle/
local.properties

# Signing material. Regenerate with the command in HANDOFF.md.
keystore/*.jks
keystore/keystore.properties

# Scratch
*.log
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Debug APKs are 14 MB each and rebuildable; releases and their R8 mapping
# are kept because a release stack trace is unreadable without the mapping.
artifacts/*-debug.apk
.impeccable/

# Working briefs and the local tooling that goes with them. These are notes and
# instructions written to a tool, not documentation of the project, and the
# repository is public. Kept locally, never committed.
#
# The pattern is deliberately not NIGHTBELL_*.md. Scripts belong in here too, and a
# NIGHTBELL_*.sh was one `git add` away from being public before this was widened.
NIGHTBELL_*

# The launch checklist annotates each task with which of them needs a human and
# which does not, in terms of the tool that was doing the other half. That is the
# same category as the briefs above, so it stays local until it is rewritten as
# plain project documentation. The content is worth keeping; the framing is not.
docs/GROWTH.md

# Unlaunched go-to-market material: the Show HN draft, the Reddit posts, the SEO
# content plan. Nothing in here is embarrassing, it is simply worth more unposted
# than it is sitting in a public repository before any of it has run.
docs/growth-prep/

# The video project, not the video.
#
# promo-video/ is a Remotion cut that renders one 40 second file. It is 52 MB
# before node_modules and 50 MB of that is audio/build: three 11 MB intermediate
# WAVs and a trim directory that exist only between a render and a mix. Its own
# .gitignore covers build/ at its root, which does not match audio/build/, so
# excluding the project here is what actually keeps that out of history. Git
# history is permanent and a 50 MB mistake cannot be taken back out of a clone.
#
# What ships is the result, committed under docs/video and copied into the site
# by `website/npm run assets`:
#
#   docs/video/nightbell-promo.mp4          40 s, the film in the hero
#   docs/video/nightbell-alert-firing.mp4   11 s, the payoff cut
#
# Rebuilding the film needs the project restored from a local copy. Rebuilding
# the site does not, which is the only reproducibility that matters here.
promo-video/

# Superseded by nightbell-promo.mp4 before the rename. 7.9 MB, referenced by
# nothing, and no reason to put it in history now.
docs/video/pulse-promo-extended.mp4

# Bytecode for the two generators in docs/brand. Regenerated on every run and
# stamped with the interpreter version, so it is noise that conflicts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.hermes/

# Kotlin build daemon session files.
.kotlin/

# Debug builds handed out during development. Rebuildable, 16 MB each.
artifacts/dev/

# Local credentials. Never committed: the key in here is live, and a secret that
# reaches a public history is burned whether or not it is removed afterwards.
.env
